<link rel="stylesheet" href="/s-13vep8.css"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://nclexsim.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"NCLEX remediation for nursing programs","item":"https://nclexsim.com/nclex-remediation-for-nursing-programs"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Vexcura: Bring your scores for nursing programs","description":"Turns outside NCLEX-readiness assessment results into assigned remediation and a remediation record. Works alongside ATI, HESI, Kaplan and UWorld; not affiliated with them.","url":"https://nclexsim.com/nclex-remediation-for-nursing-programs","applicationCategory":"EducationalApplication","operatingSystem":"Any (web browser)","offers":[{"@type":"Offer","name":"Vexcura Per student","price":"99","priceCurrency":"USD","description":"Any size; the program chooses the number of seats (per student seat), per year. Every plan includes every feature."},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Vexcura Site 100","price":"7500","priceCurrency":"USD","description":"Up to 100 students, per year. Every plan includes every feature."},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Vexcura Site 250","price":"15000","priceCurrency":"USD","description":"101 to 250 students, per year. Every plan includes every feature."},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Vexcura Site 500","price":"25000","priceCurrency":"USD","description":"251 to 500 students, per year. Every plan includes every feature."}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to import a cohort's outside assessment results into Vexcura","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"text":"Open the instructor workspace and choose Outside scores, then Import results."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"text":"Pick the test maker, the assessment name and the date."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"text":"Choose the CSV or Excel export; Vexcura reads it in your browser and previews which rows matched your students."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"text":"Save the import; students see their result and the weak-topic summary updates."}],"url":"https://nclexsim.com/nclex-remediation-for-nursing-programs"}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can we import a whole cohort's results?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Use the CSV or Excel export from your assessment vendor's site, up to 600 rows at a time. The file is read in the instructor's browser and only the matched scores are sent. Rows match students by email, or by name within your program, and rows that don't match are listed with the reason. You can remove an import later."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's in the remediation record?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For each student and outside result: the test maker, assessment, date, score, proficiency level or predicted probability, topics to review, the Vexcura study areas they map to, remediation items assigned and completed with dates, who assigned them, and Vexcura practice accuracy in that area. Download it as a CSV or print it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can see imported results?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Results your program imports are visible to your program's instructors and program admins and to the student they describe. Results a student adds are visible to your instructors only when the student shares them. Instructors at other programs never see them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Vexcura replace ATI, HESI or Kaplan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Vexcura doesn't give or score proctored exams and doesn't reproduce any vendor's questions or reports. It works alongside them: it turns the topics those reports list into practice and gives you a record of the remediation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do we need vendor logins or an integration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Vexcura never asks for vendor usernames or passwords and doesn't connect to vendor systems. Students upload or type their reports, and faculty import the export file."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is board-ready reporting available?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It's coming soon and will be included in every plan. Today you can export the remediation record as a CSV or print it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does it cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every plan includes everything, Bring your scores included. Plans start at $99 per student seat per year. Students and instructors are free."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does Vexcura's cost compare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Typical published prices, as of November 2026, are about $110–$145 per student per year for an academic EHR seat, about $35–$140 for clinical tracking, and about $229–$389 for a supplemental NCLEX review layer, and students often pay these fees themselves. Vexcura's license works out to $50–$99 per student per year depending on program size, includes an academic EHR, clinical days and attendance, and NCLEX practice, and is free for students and instructors. It doesn't replace proctored assessments. Your costs may differ; the sources are listed on this page."}}]}</script></head><body><header class="top"><div class="w"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Vexcura home"><svg class="vxw" viewBox="-2 -86 472 96" aria-hidden="true"><style>@property --vxa{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#4b4f86}@property --vxb{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#d77a6a}@property --vxc{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#f8c27a}@property --vxrb{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#f8c27a}@property --vxrc{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#d77a6a}:r