.vx-scale{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,220px),1fr));gap:8px 18px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:12px 0}.vx-scale li{line-height:1.35}.vx-scale b{color:var(--accent)}
.vx-fn{font-size:14px}.vx-fn td,.vx-fn th{padding:6px 8px}.vx-fn a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.vx-strip{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:30px 0}
.vx-strip h2{font-size:clamp(22px,3.2vw,28px);margin:0 0 6px}.vx-strip ul{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:10px 0}
.vx-strip li{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:14.5px}.vx-strip li b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.vx-strip p{margin:6px 0}</style><section class="vx-val" id="value"><h2>What programs typically pay elsewhere, and what Vexcura costs</h2>
    <p class="lead2"><b>One license covers what schools usually buy as separate tools, and it's free for every student and instructor.</b> Schools and students usually pay for an academic EHR, clinical tracking and an NCLEX review layer separately. Vexcura includes all three kinds of tool in every plan.</p>
    <div class="vx-cmp"><div><b>Academic EHR seat</b><span class="amt">about $110–$145</span><small>per student per year; published list prices</small></div><div><b>Clinical day and attendance tracking</b><span class="amt">about $35–$140</span><small>per student per year; student fees published by schools, with one-time fees spread over a two-year program</small></div><div><b>Supplemental NCLEX review layer</b><span class="amt">about $229–$389</span><small>per student per year; published retail prices for a per-student NCLEX question bank (90 to 360 days)</small></div><div class="vx-us"><b>Vexcura, every tool included</b><span class="amt">$50–$99</span><small>per student per year, depending on program size. Free for students and instructors.</small></div></div><div class="vx-calc" data-vxc='{&quot;rows&quot;:[{&quot;k&quot;:&quot;ehr&quot;,&quot;lo&quot;:110,&quot;hi&quot;:145},{&quot;k&quot;:&quot;clin&quot;,&quot;lo&quot;:35,&quot;hi&quot;:140},{&quot;k&quot;:&quot;nclex&quot;,&quot;lo&quot;:229,&quot;hi&quot;:389}],&quot;seat&quot;:99,&quot;seatName&quot;:&quot;Per student&quot;,&quot;sites&quot;:[{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 100&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:7500,&quot;m&quot;:100},{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 250&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:15000,&quot;m&quot;:250},{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 500&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:25000,&quot;m&quot;:500}],&quot;cap&quot;:500,&quot;custom&quot;:&quot;Custom quote&quot;}'><h3>Estimate your program's cost</h3>
    <div class="vc-in"><label for="vxc-n">Students in your program</label><input type="range" id="vxc-r" min="10" max="500" step="5" value="100" aria-label="Students in your program"><input type="number" id="vxc-n" min="1" max="1000" value="100" inputmode="numeric"></div>
    <fieldset><legend>Separate tools to compare</legend><label><input type="checkbox" data-vxc-k="ehr" checked> Academic EHR seat</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-vxc-k="clin" checked> Clinical day and attendance tracking</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-vxc-k="nclex" checked> Supplemental NCLEX review layer</label></fieldset>
    <div class="vx-out" aria-live="polite"><div><span>Typical separate tools, per year</span><output id="vxc-o">$37,400–$67,400</output><small>estimate from typical published prices</small></div><div><span>Vexcura, per year</span><output id="vxc-v">$7,500</output><small id="vxc-vp">Site 100 · $75 per student</small></div><div><span>Estimated difference, per year</span><output id="vxc-s">$29,900–$59,900</output><small>an estimate, not a guarantee</small></div></div>
    <p class="vx-note">Typical published prices as of November 2026; your costs may differ. Many of these fees are charged to students; with Vexcura, students pay nothing. Proctored assessments are a separate cost that Vexcura doesn't replace.</p></div>
    <script>(function(){var w=document.querySelector(".vx-calc");if(!w)return;var C=JSON.parse(w.getAttribute("data-vxc")),r=w.querySelector("#vxc-r"),n=w.querySelector("#vxc-n");
    function m(x){return "$"+Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en-US")}
    function best(k){var o=[];if(C.seat)o.push({n:C.seatName,t:C.seat*k});C.sites.forEach(function(s){if(s.m>=k)o.push({n:s.n,t:s.p})});o.sort(function(a,b){return a.t-b.t});return o[0]}
    function go(src){var k=Math.max(1,Math.round(+(src||n).value||0));if(src===r)n.value=k;else r.value=Math.min(C.cap,Math.max(10,k));var lo=0,hi=0;w.querySelectorAll("[data-vxc-k]").forEach(function(c){if(!c.checked)return;C.rows.forEach(function(x){if(x.k===c.getAttribute("data-vxc-k")){lo+=x.lo;hi+=x.hi}})});
     w.querySelector("#vxc-o").textContent=lo?m(lo*k)+"–"+m(hi*k):"$0";var b=k>C.cap?null:best(k),v=w.querySelector("#vxc-v"),vp=w.querySelector("#vxc-vp"),s=w.querySelector("#vxc-s");
     if(!b){v.textContent=C.custom;vp.textContent="More than "+C.cap+" students";s.textContent="Ask for a quote";return}
     v.textContent=m(b.t);vp.textContent=b.n+" · "+m(b.t/k)+" per student";var a=lo*k-b.t,z=hi*k-b.t;s.textContent=(lo?(a<0?"−"+m(-a):m(a))+"–"+(z<0?"−"+m(-z):m(z)):"—")}
    r.addEventListener("input",function(){go(r)});n.addEventListener("input",function(){go(n)});w.querySelectorAll("[data-vxc-k]").forEach(function(c){c.addEventListener("change",function(){go(n)})})})();</script>
    <h3>What that works out to per student</h3><div class="tw"><table class="vx-ps"><thead><tr><th>Students</th><th>Plan</th><th>Per year</th><th>Per student</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>60</td><td>Per student</td><td>$5,940</td><td><b>$99</b></td></tr><tr><td>100</td><td>Site 100</td><td>$7,500</td><td><b>$75</b></td></tr><tr><td>250</td><td>Site 250</td><td>$15,000</td><td><b>$60</b></td></tr><tr><td>500</td><td>Site 500</td><td>$25,000</td><td><b>$50</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    
    <details class="vx-src"><summary>Sources for these figures</summary><div class="tw"><table class="vx-fn"><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Product</th><th>Published price</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Academic EHR seat</td><td>EHR Go: Student subscription</td><td>$128 (12 months); $113 (40-week academic year)</td><td><a href="https://ehrgo.com/faq/" rel="nofollow noopener">Vendor FAQ</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Academic EHR seat</td><td>Wolters Kluwer (Lippincott): DocuCare, 6-month access</td><td>$71.99 per 6 months</td><td><a href="https://shop.lww.com/p/9781451187182" rel="nofollow noopener">Vendor store</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Academic EHR seat</td><td>Elsevier: SimChart (nursing)</td><td>About $139 per year</td><td><a href="https://blog.chartflow.io/posts/educational-ehr-pricing-guide-2026" rel="nofollow noopener">Secondary source (an EHR vendor's pricing guide)</a>, Article dated Aug 10, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical day and attendance tracking</td><td>Typhon Group: Clinical tracking (student fee)</td><td>$70 one-time</td><td><a href="https://webcdn.worcester.edu/nursing/wp-content/uploads/sites/18/2025/02/Student-Costs_-Lab-Clinical-Rotations.pdf" rel="nofollow noopener">Worcester State University cost sheet</a>, Uploaded Feb 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical day and attendance tracking</td><td>Typhon Group: Clinical hour tracking (graduate student fee)</td><td>$100 one-time</td><td><a href="https://www.downstate.edu/education-training/college-of-nursing/_documents/20242025graduateprogramfees.pdf" rel="nofollow noopener">SUNY Downstate 2024–2025 fees</a>, 2024–2025</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical day and attendance tracking</td><td>ProjectConcert: Student fee</td><td>$122 per year, plus $50 practicum validation</td><td><a href="https://wichita.edu/academics/health_professions/nursing/costofattendance.php" rel="nofollow noopener">Wichita State cost of attendance</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical day and attendance tracking</td><td>Exxat: Prism and Approve (student fees)</td><td>$210 one-time, plus $36 per year</td><td><a href="https://www.sc.edu/study/colleges_schools/nursing/internal/current_students/undergraduate_students/bsnstartupcosts.php" rel="nofollow noopener">University of South Carolina BSN start-up costs</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical day and attendance tracking</td><td>ACEMAPP: Collaborate and Assure (student fees)</td><td>$50 per year, plus $35 one-time</td><td><a href="https://nursing.msu.edu/student-resources/compliance" rel="nofollow noopener">Michigan State College of Nursing</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Supplemental NCLEX review layer</td><td>UWorld: NCLEX-RN review, individual retail</td><td>$229 (90 days); $389 (360 days)</td><td><a href="https://nursing.uworld.com/nclex-rn/" rel="nofollow noopener">Vendor page</a>, Accessed Nov 4, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="vx-note">Ranges are per student per year. One-time fees are spread over a two-year program. Prices are as published by the vendor or by a school passing the fee to students, on the dates shown; one figure comes from a secondary source and is labeled. Institutional contract prices are often not public. Typical published prices as of November 2026; your costs may differ. Named products are listed only as price references; Vexcura is not affiliated with any of them.</p>
    <ul class="vx-note"><li><b>Academic EHR seat:</b> Vexcura includes an Epic-style academic EHR: My Chart, MAR, flowsheets, orders, LDAs, care plans and handoff.</li><li><b>Clinical day and attendance tracking:</b> Vexcura includes clinical days with attendance, badge sign-in and assigned work. It doesn't do placement or compliance management, such as background checks and immunization records.</li><li><b>Supplemental NCLEX review layer:</b> Vexcura includes cited NCLEX-RN practice questions, new ones daily, the full adaptive practice exam and NGN case studies. It isn't a proctored assessment program and doesn't replace one.</li></ul></details><p class="vx-note">Vexcura is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by ATI (Assessment Technologies Institute), Elsevier/HESI, Kaplan or UWorld. All trademarks belong to their owners.</p></section>
    <h2 id="pricing">Every plan includes everything</h2>
    <p>Bring your scores isn't an add-on. <b>Students and instructors never pay</b>; the school or facility licenses Vexcura, and plans differ only in how many students they cover.</p>
    <div class="tw"><table class="price"><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Students</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Per student</b></td><td>Any size; the program chooses the number of seats</td><td><b>$99 per student seat</b> <small>per year</small></td></tr><tr><td><b>Site 100</b></td><td>Up to 100 students</td><td><b>$7,500</b> <small>per year</small></td></tr><tr><td><b>Site 250</b></td><td>101 to 250 students</td><td><b>$15,000</b> <small>per year</small></td></tr><tr><td><b>Site 500</b></td><td>251 to 500 students</td><td><b>$25,000</b> <small>per year</small></td></tr><tr><td><b>Custom</b></td><td>More than 500 students, several campuses, or major customizations</td><td><b>Custom quote</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="soon"><b>Coming soon:</b> board-ready reporting, included in every plan.</p>
    <h3>Every plan includes</h3><ul class="incl"><li>NCLEX-RN practice questions and adaptive practice exams, with rationales and sources</li><li>Next Generation NCLEX item types and unfolding case studies</li><li>Topic drills, bedside simulation and the ACLS megacode simulator</li><li>Missed-question cards, question of the day with streaks, and results by category</li><li>The academic EHR: My Chart, MAR, flowsheets, orders, LDAs, care plans and handoff</li><li>The Brain and worklist sidebar, with assigned work and required documentation</li><li>Live clinical groups with patients students choose to share</li><li>The instructor workspace: my students, clinical days with attendance, assign work, curriculum and content</li><li>Bring your scores: outside score reports turned into study plans, cohort import and the remediation record</li><li>Program admin: seats, codes, rosters and a data export</li><li>Badge sign-in with any USB RFID or barcode reader, with an optional PIN</li><li>Your own curriculum uploads, shown next to Vexcura content</li><li>Google and Microsoft sign-in, and LTI 1.3 for your LMS</li><li>Free printable study guides and PDFs</li><li>Setup help from Tyler Savage, RN</li></ul>
    <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a free semester pilot</a><a class="btn alt" href="tel:+17626772802">Call 762-677-2802</a></div>
    <h2>Questions programs ask</h2><details class="faq"><summary>Can we import a whole cohort's results?</summary><p>Yes. Use the CSV or Excel export from your assessment vendor's site, up to 600 rows at a time. The file is read in the instructor's browser and only the matched scores are sent. Rows match students by email, or by name within your program, and rows that don't match are listed with the reason. You can remove an import later.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What's in the remediation record?</summary><p>For each student and outside result: the test maker, assessment, date, score, proficiency level or predicted probability, topics to review, the Vexcura study areas they map to, remediation items assigned and completed with dates, who assigned them, and Vexcura practice accuracy in that area. Download it as a CSV or print it.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Who can see imported results?</summary><p>Results your program imports are visible to your program's instructors and program admins and to the student they describe. Results a student adds are visible to your instructors only when the student shares them. Instructors at other programs never see them.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does Vexcura replace ATI, HESI or Kaplan?</summary><p>No. Vexcura doesn't give or score proctored exams and doesn't reproduce any vendor's questions or reports. It works alongside them: it turns the topics those reports list into practice and gives you a record of the remediation.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Do we need vendor logins or an integration?</summary><p>No. Vexcura never asks for vendor usernames or passwords and doesn't connect to vendor systems. Students upload or type their reports, and faculty import the export file.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Is board-ready reporting available?</summary><p>It's coming soon and will be included in every plan. Today you can export the remediation record as a CSV or print it.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What does it cost?</summary><p>Every plan includes everything, Bring your scores included. Plans start at $99 per student seat per year. Students and instructors are free.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How does Vexcura's cost compare?</summary><p>Typical published prices, as of November 2026, are about $110–$145 per student per year for an academic EHR seat, about $35–$140 for clinical tracking, and about $229–$389 for a supplemental NCLEX review layer, and students often pay these fees themselves. Vexcura's license works out to $50–$99 per student per year depending on program size, includes an academic EHR, clinical days and attendance, and NCLEX practice, and is free for students and instructors. It doesn't replace proctored assessments. Your costs may differ; the sources are listed on this page.</p></details>
